{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PlanckStepAtomicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PlanckStepAtomicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClockUniqueness"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.borel_identification_core_of_atomicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.borel_identification_core_of_atomicity","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L259-L280","doc":"**The merged chain end-to-end (proved, sorry-free, conditional).**\nATOMICITY of the substrate computation monoid + the P2 clock premises\n(`hb`, `hs`) + shared-variable representability `hrep` (OPEN) + the\nLean-proved keystone identity `hkey` (`KeystoneBridgeC1Binding`, per the\n`_of_` discipline) ⇒ the binding normalizer is the unit factorial\nsequence `N(m+1) = m!` — the arithmetic core of\n`conj:schwinger-measure-computational-time` (`moment_eq_normalizer` at\nunit `ς = 1`). The SCU hypothesis of `borel_identification_core` is\ndischarged through the atomicity instance above, so the deepest open\nstructural premise on this route is now `PlanckStepAtomicity` itself.\nNOT supplied (unchanged honest residual): the analytic fields\n(`positive`, `integrable`) of the (REP) class and the classical\nCarleman–Stieltjes determinacy theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.substrateClockUniqueness_of_planckStepAtomicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.substrateClockUniqueness_of_planckStepAtomicity","kind":"instance","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L241-L257","doc":"**Conditional discharge of SCU (proved, sorry-free; §3b dependent\npattern).** GIVEN Planck-step atomicity, substrate clock uniqueness\nHOLDS: `[PlanckStepAtomicity M] → SubstrateClockUniqueness M K`, by the\nproved discharge map `unique_up_to_scale_of_atomic` (only the generation\nclause is consumed; freeness backs the remark's well-defined-count\nclaim). Stated as an INSTANCE — honest precisely because the premise\nclass has NO instance, so nothing fires unconditionally: SCU (and, via\n`clocks_agree_up_to_scale` / `borel_identification_core`, the whole\nclock-level reduction) becomes available exactly in contexts that\nexplicitly assume atomicity. This does not close SCU; it relocates its\nentire content into `PlanckStepAtomicity`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomicity_fails_for_two_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomicity_fails_for_two_generators","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L197-L239","doc":"**Non-tautology witness (proved, unconditional).** Atomicity FAILS\nfor the rank-two step monoid `ℕ × ℕ`: no single element generates it.\nHence `PlanckStepAtomicity` carries real content — it asserts the\nsubstrate's computation does not decompose into independent parallel\nstep-counting directions. (Well-foundedness of the computation order\ndoes NOT imply this: `ℕ × ℕ` is well-founded under lex order yet not\natomic — which is why `prop:ordering-jet-compatibility`'s proved\nwell-foundedness cannot discharge the class.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.exists_indivisible_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.exists_indivisible_generator","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L186-L195","doc":"Class-level packaging: an atomic computation monoid has a nonzero,\nindivisible generator whose iterates exhaust it — the class genuinely\nencodes \"one indivisible Planck step\", not a weaker shadow of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.stepIterate_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.stepIterate_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L174-L184","doc":"**The computation monoid is a copy of `ℕ`.** For an atomic generator\nthe iterate map `n ↦ n • g` is a bijection `ℕ → M` (injective by\nfreeness, surjective by generation) — the precise sense of the\nmission-level phrasing \"the substrate computation monoid ≅ ℕ, generated\nby a single indivisible step\". (It is additive by `add_nsmul`, so this\nis a monoid isomorphism onto `M`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomic_generator_indivisible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomic_generator_indivisible","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L153-L172","doc":"**No half-step (derived).** The generator of an atomic computation\nmonoid is INDIVISIBLE: any decomposition `a + b = g` has `a = 0` or\n`b = 0`. This is the literal \"there is no sub-step resolution\" of\n`rem:discrete-planck-step`, derived from generation + freeness rather\nthan assumed separately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomic_generator_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.atomic_generator_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L144-L151","doc":"A free generator is not the empty computation: `g ≠ 0`. (If `g = 0`\nthen `1 • g = 0 • g`, so freeness forces `1 = 0` in `ℕ`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity.atomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity.atomic","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L140-L140","doc":"There is one Planck step generating every computation segment,\nwith pairwise-distinct iterates: no sub-step resolution, well-defined\nstep count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.PlanckStepAtomicity","kind":"class","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PlanckStepAtomicity.lean#L114-L142","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — NO instance; §3b-tax).** ATOMICITY of\nthe substrate's computation monoid — the formal content of\n`rem:discrete-planck-step`'s \"there is no sub-step resolution\": there is\na single step `g` (one full Reeb circuit, the Planck step) such that\n\n* every computation segment is an iterate `n • g` of it (`generates` —\n  nothing exists between the iterates, no sub-step), and\n* distinct iterate counts give distinct segments (`free` — \"the count of\n  Planck steps measures dynamical distance\": counting is well defined).\n\nEquivalently `n ↦ n • g` is an additive bijection `ℕ ≃ M`\n(`stepIterate_bijective`): the computation monoid is a copy of `ℕ`\ngenerated by one indivisible step (indivisibility is DERIVED:\n`atomic_generator_indivisible`). This is a genuine structural\nrestriction — FALSE for the rank-two step monoid `ℕ × ℕ`\n(`atomicity_fails_for_two_generators`). The corpus's ℕ-valued\n`InformationTheoreticTime.stepCount` is a chart reading OF this\nconjecture (a modeling choice), not a proof of it; an instance may only\nbe created from a genuine derivation of the computation order's\nrank-one/ℕ-shape (open). ","signatureChunk":0}]}